S_k = 1^3 + 3^3 + \dots + (2k - 1)^3 = \left(\frac{2k (2k - 1)}{2}\right)^2 = k^2 (2k - 1)^2
\]Then we must compute $S_k$: \begin{align*}
S_k & = 0^2 \cdot (-1)^2 + 1^2 \cdot (1)^2 + \dots + k^2 \cdot (2k - 1)^2 \\
& = \frac{k(k + 1) \cdot 2k(2k + 1) \cdot (4k^2 - 2k - 1)}{3}
\end{align*}So we find \[
S_k = \frac{(2k^2 + k)(8k^3 - 6k^2 - 2k)}{3}
\]and use this to find \[
